_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id                   1E66 
_pdbx_entry_details.compound_details           
;HYDROLYZES CHOLINE RELEASED INTO THE SYNAPSE.
 CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ACETYLCHOLINE + H(2)O = CHOLINE + ACETATE.
 INHIBITORS OF THE ENZYME ACETYLCHOLINESTERASE (ACHE) SLOW AND
 SOMETIMES REVERSE THE COGNITIVE DECLINE EXPERIENCED BY INDIVIDUALS
 WITH ALZHEIMER'S DISEASE. HUPERZINE A, A NATURAL PRODUCT USED IN
 TRADITIONAL CHINESE HERBAL MEDICINE, AND TACRINE (COGNEX) ARE AMONG
 THE POTENT ACHE INHIBITORS USED IN THIS TREATMENT.
 (-)-12-AMINO-3-CHLORO-9-ETHYL-6,7,10,11-TETRAHYDRO-7,11-
 METHANOCYCLOOCTA[B]QUINOLINE HYDROCHLORIDE (HUPRINE X), A HYBRID
 THAT COMBINES THE CARBOBICYCLIC SUBSTRUCTURE OF HUPERZINE A
 WITH WITH THE 4-AMINOQUINOLINE SUBSTRUCTURE OF TACRINE HUPRINE X
 BINDS TO HUMAN ACHE WITH AN INHIBITION CONSTANT K(I) OF 26 PM.
 HUPRINE X SHOWS NO DETECTABLE AFFINITY FOR THE EDROPHONIUM-ACHE
 COMPLEX. HUPRINE X BINDS  TO THE ENZYME ACYLATION SITE IN THE
 ACTIVE SITE GORGE INTERFERES SLIGHTLY WITH THE BINDING OF
 PERIPHERAL SITE LIGANDS.
;
